WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.197
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:07.670 --> 00:00:11.440
SPEAKER: Bank robberies,
military compounds, and spies--

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:13.120
that's what you might
think of when it

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:14.740
comes to data center security.

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:17.320
And to be honest,
you're not too far off.

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:19.600
But how exactly
does Google reliably

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:21.550
secure its data centers?

00:00:21.550 --> 00:00:26.350
It all starts with six layers,
also known as Defense in Depth.

00:00:26.350 --> 00:00:29.860
Layers become progressively more
protected with access checks

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:32.170
as you move to the core
of the data center.

00:00:32.170 --> 00:00:34.810
Layers one and two involve
property boundaries,

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:38.290
vehicle crash barriers,
fences with motion detection,

00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:41.140
guard kiosks, and
thermal cameras.

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:43.960
Layer three gives you
access to the secure lobby,

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:47.410
where you get your irises
scanned, and will find

00:00:47.410 --> 00:00:50.500
the general office area where
hardware and data center

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:52.330
operations teams work.

00:00:52.330 --> 00:00:54.820
You're now in the
data center building.

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:57.670
Badge checks exist
at every entry point,

00:00:57.670 --> 00:01:01.240
and only one person can go
through a door at a time.

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:03.070
As you move to
layer four, you'll

00:01:03.070 --> 00:01:07.090
find operational rooms, like the
core network room and security

00:01:07.090 --> 00:01:10.510
operations center, which
contains a highly trained staff

00:01:10.510 --> 00:01:13.000
that monitors all
aspects of security

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:16.060
and can keep a level
head at all times.

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:19.120
Next is layer five,
the data center floor.

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:22.820
Less than 1% of Googlers
ever get to set foot here.

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:24.730
This is where data lives.

00:01:24.730 --> 00:01:27.410
In order to advance, you
have to walk through a circle

00:01:27.410 --> 00:01:31.120
lock, a big glass tube that
lets only one person enter

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:32.080
at a time.

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:34.300
Here, you get your
credentials checked

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:36.190
and your irises scanned.

00:01:36.190 --> 00:01:39.130
This is a form of
dual-factor authentication.

00:01:39.130 --> 00:01:42.550
You must present two forms of
identification-- in this case,

00:01:42.550 --> 00:01:44.440
a badge and biometric data--

00:01:44.440 --> 00:01:47.290
to validate an
individual's identity.

00:01:47.290 --> 00:01:50.830
Layer six is disk erase,
where retiring hard drives

00:01:50.830 --> 00:01:55.090
get their data wiped and reused
or shredded and recycled.

00:01:55.090 --> 00:01:57.340
Only those with
special access can

00:01:57.340 --> 00:01:59.815
enter the disk erase
room and retrieve drives

00:01:59.815 --> 00:02:02.230
through a secure
two-way locker system.

00:02:02.230 --> 00:02:04.510
In order to exit
layers five and six,

00:02:04.510 --> 00:02:06.730
you're required to go
through full metal detection

00:02:06.730 --> 00:02:09.130
under the supervision
of a staff member.

00:02:09.130 --> 00:02:11.740
But what about protecting
from the outside?

00:02:11.740 --> 00:02:16.120
We're talking asteroids,
electromagnetic pulses, fires,

00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:18.790
pandemics, and zombies.

00:02:18.790 --> 00:02:21.160
We run dozens of
drills a year, engaging

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:24.940
unannounced skilled adversaries
to try to get past controls.

00:02:24.940 --> 00:02:27.250
After every testing
attempt, we always

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:29.260
evaluate our
performance to ensure

00:02:29.260 --> 00:02:31.150
the strength of our
security controls

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:33.350
and iterate controls, as needed.

00:02:33.350 --> 00:02:36.040
Now, that's what you call
a culture of security.

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:40.690
If you want to learn more, check
out cloud.google.com/security.

00:02:40.690 --> 00:02:44.040
[MUSIC PLAYING]

